==Trivia==
*The Lava Hound is based on the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basset_Hound basset hound], which has an average litter of 6 to 8 pups and the Lava Hound, when defeated, releases a total of 6 Lava Pups.
*The Lava Hound is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The Lava Hound resembles the Level 1-2 Lava Hound from Clash of Clans.
**He functions just like his [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Lava_Hound Clash of Clans counterpart], but when he is upgraded in Clash Royale, the Lava Pups gain a stat increase, while in Clash of Clans the Lava Pups gain a count increase.
**Unlike in Clash of Clans, the Lava Hound in Clash Royale does not have death damage and does not prioritize any specific building.
**In Clash of Clans, his movement speed is high whereas in Clash Royale, his movement speed is low.
*The Lava Hound, along with Mega Knight, is the most expensive permanent {{Rarity|Legendary}} card, costing 7 [[Elixir]].
*The Lava Hound is one of the first troop [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, [[Knight]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Lava Pups are 1 of 9 troops that have the same sprite for both players, the others are Skeletons, [[Electro Spirit]], [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Heal Spirit]], Elixir Blob, and Phoenix.
*The Lava Hound is the first card to have its own Super Troop version.
*In the Italian and French language settings of the game, the Lava Hound's name translates to "Lava Mastiff" meanwhile in the Russian language settings of the game,  it translates to "Hell Hound"
*The Lava Hound bears more than a passing resemblance to [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Heatran_(Pok%C3%A9mon) Heatran] from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon Pokemon].
*The Lava Hound is confirmed to be a male, as the storyteller in [https://youtu.be/5fbKJG_4qRo?t=29 The Last Lava Pup commercial] referred to Lava Hound as "he" and "father".
*While the Lava Hound appears to be made of both molten lava and solid rock, the Lava Pup seems to be a pure lava being. Fans theorize that the lava cools into rocks as the Lava Pups mature.
*It appears to have an underbite, similar to the Minions, [[Guards]], Giant Skeleton, and Super Lava Hound.
*A large part of the Lava Hound's card description is used as a [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]].
*The Lava Hound is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays it, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, P.E.K.K.A., Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], Goblin Giant, Golem, Bowler, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Sparky]], Night Witch, [[Super Lava Hound]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Lava Hound, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], Ice Spirit, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Dart Goblin, Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], Guards, Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, Golem, Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, Inferno Dragon, and Royal Ghost, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Lava Hound is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Lava Hound does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*The Lava Pups' range was shown as 2 before the [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/1/2020)|7/1/2020 balance changes]].
*The Lava Hound was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/Sa0QOSJ5AVY?si=Hlcj6efCnFhxfDYe Clash Royale League 2024 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.

